  "merger_description": "Syngenta Crop Protection AG (**SCPAG**) and the\u00a0D\u00fcmmen Orange Group (**D\u00fcmmen Orange**) propose to enter a joint venture to combine their global ornamental plant breeding and propagation businesses.\n\nSCPAG is\u00a0a Swiss agribusiness that operates in the crop protection and seeds markets in Australia and internationally. In Australia, SCPAG operates through its wholly owned subsidiary, Syngenta APP Assets, selling and distributing seeds for annuals, perennials, and pot plants.\n\nD\u00fcmmen Orange is a global horticultural company that operates in breeding and propagation of flowers and plants.\u00a0In Australia, D\u00fcmmen\u00a0Orange\u2019s primary activity is the licensing of plant genetics under the\u00a0D\u00fcmmen Orange\u00a0brand. D\u00fcmmen\u00a0Orange also supplies cuttings and in vitro materials for annuals, perennials, pot plants and cut flowers.",
